# Razer Mouse Dock Pro (1532:00a4). Installed by `sudo make install-udev` (and
# `sudo make install-daemon`), which also creates the razerd group.
#
# 1. Let members of the razerd system group open its hidraw nodes, so `razerd`
#    and razerd-watch.service need no root. A group rather than TAG+="uaccess":
#    the ACL uaccess grants only exists while you have an active seat session,
#    and a lingering razerd-watch.service started at boot would have no access
#    until you log in.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="1532", ATTR{idProduct}=="00a4", GROUP="razerd", MODE="0660"
KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1532", ATTRS{idProduct}=="00a4", GROUP="razerd", MODE="0660"
#
# 2. Hand the control interface — USB interface 0, the one node razerd talks
#    to — to systemd as a device unit, and have it pull razerd.service in. The
#    symlink gives the unit a stable name, dev-razer\x2ddock.device, for the
#    BindsTo= in the service: it starts when the dock is plugged in or found at
#    boot, and stops when the dock goes. ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM is set by the
#    usb_id import of 60-persistent-hidraw.rules, which sorts before this file;
#    the two ATTRS keys sit on the same parent (the USB device), as udev wants.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1532", ATTRS{idProduct}=="00a4", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="00", SYMLINK+="razer-dock", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="razerd.service"
